Patient-Robot Instructions: Physical AI Oncology Trials
======================================================
LaTeX Source Code and Compiled PDF

Files
-----
- patient_robot_instructions.tex   Main LaTeX document (10 pages)
- patient_robot_instructions.sty   Custom style package
- references.bib                   BibTeX bibliography (35 references)
- README                           This file

Compilation
-----------
To compile the LaTeX source:

    pdflatex patient_robot_instructions.tex
    bibtex patient_robot_instructions
    pdflatex patient_robot_instructions.tex
    pdflatex patient_robot_instructions.tex

Or with latexmk:

    latexmk -pdf patient_robot_instructions.tex

Requirements: texlive-latex-base, texlive-latex-extra, texlive-fonts-recommended,
              texlive-pictures (for TikZ)

Note on Illustrations
---------------------
The compiled PDF (Patient-Robot Instructions: Physical AI Oncology Trials.pdf) was
generated using Python Cairo for high-resolution vector illustrations. The .tex
source includes placeholder illustration descriptions that correspond to the Cairo-
rendered images. To reproduce the full PDF with illustrations, run:

    python3 generate_pdf.py       # Generates combined 10-page PDF
    python3 generate_illustrations.py  # Generates individual SVG/PDF/PNG files

Individual illustrations are available in:
    ../svg/   (SVG vector format)
    ../pdf/   (PDF vector format)
    ../png/   (PNG raster format, 3600x4000 pixels)

Content Overview
----------------
10 pages, each a self-contained instructional sheet for one robot type:

  Page 1:  Surgical Robots
  Page 2:  Cobots (Collaborative Robots)
  Page 3:  Radiotherapy Patient-Positioning Robots
  Page 4:  Robotic Needle-Placement Systems
  Page 5:  Social Companion Robots (Pediatric)
  Page 6:  Humanoids (Pediatric)
  Page 7:  Radiotherapy Motion-Management / Tracking Robots
  Page 8:  Imaging Assistant Robots
  Page 9:  Steerable Needle / Needle-Steering Robots
  Page 10: Rehabilitation Exoskeletons / Robotic Gait Trainers

Each page includes:
  (a) Header: Author, ORCID, affiliation, email
  (b) Title: "Patient-Robot Instructions: Physical AI Oncology Trials - [Robot Type]"
  (c) Black-and-white portrait illustration of patient interacting with robot
  (d) Five instruction sections (numbered lists):
      1. Preparation at Home
      2. Entering the Room
      3. During the Interaction
      4. Concluding the Session
      5. At Home & Follow-Up
  (e) Footer: Date, DOI, AI model, page number, truncated source links

ISO Standards Referenced
------------------------
- ISO 15223-1:2021 (Medical device symbols)
- ISO 20417:2021 (Medical device information)
- ISO 7000:2019 (Graphical symbols for equipment)
- IEC 60417:2023 (Graphical symbols for equipment)
- ISO 7010:2019 (Safety signs - including W003 ionizing radiation)
- ISO 3864-1:2011 (Safety colours and safety signs)

